# Python AgentCore (Strands)

## Defaults for this monorepo

- **Framework:** [Strands Agents](https://strandsagents.com) only (Python).
- **Models:** Amazon Bedrock via AWS credentials (default model from AgentCore / Strands config).
- **Region:** `eu-west-1` (match `packages/core/src/env.ts` and SST workload region).
- **CLI:** Official [**AgentCore CLI**](https://github.com/aws/agentcore-cli) — `npm install -g @aws/agentcore` (not the legacy Python `bedrock-agentcore-starter-toolkit`).
- **Deploy:** AgentCore Runtime via `agentcore deploy` (CDK under the hood). SST deploy is separate unless you wire runtime ARN in `infra/`.

## Where code lives

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `packages/agent-core/src/agent.py` | `BedrockAgentCoreApp` entrypoint |
| `packages/agent-core/src/config.py` | Env: region, memory, MCP, system prompt |
| `packages/agent-core/src/memory.py` | `AgentCoreMemorySessionManager` (STM / optional LTM) |
| `packages/agent-core/src/mcp_tools.py` | Strands `MCPClient` (stdio MCP server) |
| `packages/functions/` | Lambdas that call Bedrock or invoke AgentCore runtime |
| `infra/` | SST — add IAM/runtime wiring only when integrating with the web stack |

## AgentCore CLI workflow

```bash
npm install -g @aws/agentcore

# New standalone project (AWS-recommended layout)
agentcore create --name MyAgent --framework Strands --model-provider Bedrock --memory none

# Or extend this monorepo's src/ and deploy from an AgentCore project rooted here
cd packages/agent-core
agentcore dev
agentcore deploy
agentcore invoke --prompt "Hello"
agentcore add memory      # then agentcore deploy
agentcore add gateway     # MCP/OpenAPI targets for production tool access
agentcore logs
agentcore traces list
```

Project layout from `agentcore create`:

```
agentcore/agentcore.json   # resources (agents, memory, gateways, …)
agentcore/aws-targets.json
app/<AgentName>/main.py    # entrypoint + pyproject.toml
```

## Conventions

- **Credentials:** IAM roles / SSO — no long-lived keys in git. Use `agentcore/` `.env.local` (gitignored) for local API keys only.
- **Python env:** `packages/agent-core/.venv` + `pip install -r requirements.txt` (`bedrock-agentcore[strands-agents]`, `mcp`).
- **Entrypoint contract:** `invoke(payload, context)` — read `prompt`, optional `session_id` / `actor_id` (or from `context.session_id` / `context.user_id` on runtime).
- **Do not** add TypeScript/LangGraph agents in this folder — keep Python Strands consistent.

## When to use Harness vs code

| Approach | Use |
|----------|-----|
| **Harness** (`agentcore add harness`) | Declarative agent (model + tools + memory) without custom loop |
| **Code (this repo)** | Custom Strands logic, MCP wiring, memory session manager |

Start with code here; move to harness only if you do not need custom orchestration.

